                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Almost.  This is a fairly good game.  The levels are laid out well and there's a good mix of a few different types.  It's a basic exploration game, looking for 3 stars per level.\n\nMinor complaint: the spawnpoints are not safe.  One death often results in two.  As there was only one level I had any trouble completing with the default number of lives, this is no big deal.\n\nUnfortunately, the control scheme is awful.  Mouse only and you move it in the direction you want your character to move.  That's a whole lot of mouse movement, with no way to adjust sensitivity.  It looks like the only good way to play the game is with a joystick.",
